It is Wednesday morning, and it is already very hot.
The sun is shining brightly over Berlin.
I walk to the station and am already sweating a little.
Now I am standing here and waiting for the U-Bahn.
My stomach is growling very loudly.
I almost always eat in the flat in the mornings.
But I had absolutely no time for breakfast today.
My alarm clock was unfortunately much too quiet this morning.
I was running late.
So I only quickly packed my laptop into the backpack.
The U-Bahn finally arrives, and I get on.
There are many people here, and the air is extremely warm.
I really do not need a jacket today.
A woman next to me has a large iced coffee.
That looks fantastic.
I am heading towards the office.
I will buy myself a Brötchen and a regular coffee on the way in a moment.
Then I am ready for work.
